Here’s the semantic interpretation of the scene based on the provided ontology vocabulary:

Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Pedestrians crossing in foggy conditions" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasActor :actor2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian .
:actor2 a :Pedestrian .

:weather1 a :FoggyCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Pedestrians crossing the road in foggy conditions increases collision risk" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .
